- name: inapp_review
  type: table
  desc: Native in-app review request for Google Play, iOS, and macOS. The
        module is present on other Defold targets but reports unsupported.
        Store policy decides whether a rating dialog actually appears.
  members:

    - name: is_supported
      type: function
      desc: Check whether this runtime can attempt an in-app review request.
            On Android this checks Android 5.0+ and an enabled Google Play Store;
            it cannot prove that the app was installed through Google Play.
            On iOS and macOS this checks StoreKit OS availability.
      returns:
        - name: supported
          type: boolean

    - name: request_review
      type: function
      desc: Ask the platform for a native review prompt. The return value only
            reports whether the extension accepted the request. The optional
            callback runs on the Defold update thread. On Android it runs when
            the Play flow ends or fails; on Apple it runs after StoreKit receives
            the request. Neither platform reports whether a dialog appeared or
            the user rated the app. Only one request can be pending at a time.
      parameters:
        - name: callback
          type: function|nil
          desc: Optional function(self, result). result.status is `finished`
                on Android flow completion, `requested` on Apple, or `error`.
                On error, result.reason is `request_failed`, `launch_failed`,
                or `not_visible`.
      returns:
        - name: accepted
          type: boolean
          desc: True when the request was accepted for processing.
        - name: reason
          type: string|nil
          desc: Nil on acceptance, otherwise `unsupported`, `busy`,
                `not_visible`, or `platform_error`.
      examples:
        - desc: |-
            ```lua
            if inapp_review.is_supported() then
                local accepted, reason = inapp_review.request_review(function(self, result)
                    if result.status == "error" then
                        print("Review request failed:", result.reason)
                    end
                end)
                if not accepted then
                    print("Review request unavailable:", reason)
                end
            end
            ```
